ces include Ruby City and Chris Park.","source_url":"https://rubycity.org/plan-your-visit/","source_title":"Plan Your Visit | Ruby City","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Free and open to the public; Ruby City is listed Thursday–Sunday, 10 a.m.–6 p.m., while Chris Park is listed Tuesday–Sunday, 10 a.m.–6 p.m.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"contemporary-at-blue-star","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Contemporary at Blue Star","title":"Explore Contemporary at Blue Star","subtitle":"116 Blue Star, Blue Star Arts Complex","notes":"Choose an exhibition day and give yourselves time to read the wall text, then use the Art Learning Lab prompts to start a low-key art conversation.","short_summary":"Free contemporary-art exhibitions in the Blue Star Arts Complex.","evidence_claim":"Contemporary at Blue Star states that admission to its exhibitions and programs is free and identifies its location in Building C of the Blue Star Arts Complex.","source_url":"https://contemporarysa.org/visit/","source_title":"Visit the Contemporary at Blue Star","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Public exhibition hours are listed Wednesday noon–5 p.m., Thursday–Friday noon–8 p.m., Saturday–Sunday 10 a.m.–6 p.m.; confirm installation closures.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"san-antonio-museum-of-art","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"San Antonio Museum of Art","title":"Use your UTSA ID at SAMA","subtitle":"200 West Jones Avenue, downtown San Antonio","notes":"Bring your current UTSA ID for a self-guided museum visit. Pick one gallery to explore together rather than trying to cover the whole collection at once.","short_summary":"UTSA community members receive free general admission with ID.","evidence_claim":"The San Antonio Museum of Art lists UTSA students, faculty, and staff among university partners who receive free general admission with school IDs.","source_url":"https://www.samuseum.org/visit/","source_title":"Visit | San Antonio Museum of Art","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Bring a UTSA school ID. Free general admission does not necessarily cover special-exhibition surcharges; the museum lists Tuesday hours through 7 p.m.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"witte-museum","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Witte Museum","title":"Schedule a Free Tuesday at the Witte","subtitle":"3801 Broadway, San Antonio","notes":"If you are a Bexar County resident, meet during the museum’s Tuesday free-admission window and focus your visit on one exhibit or the outdoor grounds.","short_summary":"A weekly no-cost museum window for Bexar County residents.","evidence_claim":"The Witte Museum states that Bexar County residents receive free general admission every Tuesday from 3 to 6 p.m.","source_url":"https://www.wittemuseum.org/plan-your-visit/free-tuesdays/","source_title":"Free Tuesday for Bexar County Residents | Witte Museum","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Free general admission is for Bexar County residents on Tuesdays, 3–6 p.m.; bring any documentation the museum requests and review current exhibit policies.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"mcnay-art-museum","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"McNay Art Museum","title":"Catch a free Thursday evening at the McNay","subtitle":"6000 North New Braunfels Avenue, San Antonio","notes":"Plan for Thursday after class and visit the main collection galleries together. Optional featured exhibitions can carry a separate charge, so stay with the free galleries.","short_summary":"Free main-collection access on Thursday evenings.","evidence_claim":"The McNay visitor guide lists free Thursday nights from 4 to 9 p.m. and free first Sundays for the main collection galleries.","source_url":"https://www.mcnayart.org/images/uploads/Visitor_Guide_FINAL.pdf","source_title":"McNay Art Museum Visitor Guide","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Free Thursday nights are listed 4–9 p.m. for main collection galleries. Featured exhibitions may have an optional additional charge.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"mission-san-jose-guided-walk","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Mission San José Guided Walk","title":"Join the Mission San José ranger-guided walk","subtitle":"Mission San José Visitor Center, San Antonio Missions National Historical Park","notes":"Arrive before the daily walk at the visitor center and follow the paved route with a friend. Bring water and respect the historic structures and marked paths.","short_summary":"A free, ranger-led introduction to Mission San José.","evidence_claim":"The National Park Service lists free daily ranger-guided walks at Mission San José at 10 a.m. and 11 a.m.; all park programs are free of charge.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/saan/planyourvisit/guided-programs.htm","source_title":"Guided Programs | San Antonio Missions National Historical Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Walks begin at the Mission San José Visitor Center, are first-come first-served, weather permitting, and limited to 50 people. No ranger programs on first Wednesdays.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"mission-concepcion-ranger-program","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Mission Concepción Ranger Program","title":"Meet a ranger at Mission Concepción","subtitle":"Mission Concepción, San Antonio Missions National Historical Park","notes":"Make Mission Concepción a daytime history outing and join the listed daily ranger program. Use the visit as a slow walk-and-talk, not a rush through the site.","short_summary":"A free daily ranger program at one of the park’s four mission sites.","evidence_claim":"The National Park Service lists a daily 10 a.m. ranger program at Mission Concepción and states that all park programs are free of charge.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/saan/planyourvisit/guided-programs.htm","source_title":"Guided Programs | San Antonio Missions National Historical Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Mission Concepción’s ranger program is listed daily at 10 a.m., weather permitting. The National Park Service says all programs are free; check updates before travel.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
